    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Released by Epitaph in 1995, Firme is one of Voodoo Glow Skulls’ defining ska-punk albums. The Riverside, California, band combines breakneck punk energy, brassy ska rhythms, melodic guitar hooks, and shouted vocals into a consistently charged set. Tracks such as “Shoot the Moon,” “Closet Monster,” “Charlie Brown,” and “Fat Randy” capture the group’s irreverent humor, sharp ensemble playing, and muscular, street-level intensity, while the seven-piece lineup gives the arrangements unusual weight and color.\n\nThe album became a high point in the band’s popularity and helped establish Voodoo Glow Skulls as an important act in the 1990s ska-punk scene. Its companion Spanish-language edition, Firme (en Español), appeared in 1996, underscoring the group’s bilingual identity and distinctive place within the genre. The Music On Vinyl edition presents the original album on 180-gram vinyl, preserving a key document of the band’s most energetic period.",
